HOW TO GET YOUR FILES BACK (Sigil recovery kit)
================================================

This folder was made on @DATE@ with @VERSION@.
It sits next to (or travels with) these archives:

@ARCHIVES@

Nothing in this kit is secret. Passphrases and identity keys (.sgk) are NOT here:
you need the passphrase (or key) the archive was sealed with, if it was locked.

1. Check the kit is untouched
   In this folder:   sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS      (macOS: shasum -a 256 -c SHA256SUMS)
   Every line must say OK. If a program fails, get a fresh copy from
   https://github.com/Dastille/Sigil-protocol/releases (source code is there too, AGPL-3.0).
   The archives as they were when this kit was made: from the folder that holds them,
     sha256sum -c sigil-recovery/ARCHIVES.sha256
   A FAILED .sg1 line means damage (go to 4b). A log folder grows after the kit was made, so
   INDEX / HEAD / new segments may differ; use step 4c (log verify) for logs instead.

2. Pick the program for this computer from bin/
@BINARIES@
   Linux/macOS: make it runnable first:   chmod +x bin/NAME
   macOS may warn about an unsigned program: right-click > Open, or build from source.

3. Look at the archive (safe, writes nothing, no passphrase)
   bin/NAME scry ARCHIVE.sg1

4a. Healthy? Open it
   bin/NAME unseal ARCHIVE.sg1 -o restored
   Locked archive: put the passphrase alone on the first line of a file only you can read
   (chmod 600 pw.txt) and add  --pass-file pw.txt   (or --identity your.sgk).
   Never type the passphrase on the command line.

4b. Damaged? Repair a copy first (no passphrase needed), then open the copy
   bin/NAME mend ARCHIVE.sg1 -o fixed.sg1
   bin/NAME mend --soft ARCHIVE.sg1 -o fixed.sg1     (scattered bit flips)
   bin/NAME unseal fixed.sg1 -o restored [--pass-file pw.txt]
   Or in one step without writing a repaired file: bin/NAME unseal --repair ...

4c. A segment log (a folder named NAME.sigil with INDEX and segments/)
   bin/NAME log verify NAME.sigil            (health; --pass-file for a private log)
   bin/NAME log mend NAME.sigil              (heal damaged segments in place)
   bin/NAME log restore NAME.sigil . -o restored [--pass-file pw.txt]

4d. Pieces spread over several sticks or folders (scatter / deluge / cold kit)
   Put all the pieces you have in one folder, then
   bin/NAME gather FOLDER -o ARCHIVE.sg1     (any k of n pieces are enough)
   Cold USB kits:  bin/NAME kit mend --help

5. No program works on this computer?
   spec/sigil-v1.txt describes the format exactly; any programmer can write a reader.
   The Sigil web lab (a browser page) can also open .sg1 files.

Run any command with --help for details.
